 34AL c  2006FuZX: a secondary cocktail beam of 28−31Na, 30−33Mg, 32−35Al,      
 34AL2c  34−36Si, 36,37P were produced via the projectile fragmentation of a    
 34AL3c  63-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam impinging on 1-mm-thick C and Be   
 34AL4c  targets and selected by the RIKEN Projectile-Fragment Separator (RIPS).
 34AL5c  The secondary cocktail beam was directed onto a 150-mg/cm{+2} liquid He
 34AL6c  target and the outgoing particles were identified by energy loss,      
 34AL7c  kinetic energy, and time-of-flight measured using a Si detector, a NaI 
 34AL8c  calorimeter, and a couple of plastic scintillators. The positions and  
 34AL9c  directions of incident and outgoing particles were measured using      
 34ALAc  PPACs. Only outgoing particles were identified so that the excited     
 34ALBc  states could be populated by any allowed reactions. Deexcited |g rays  
 34ALCc  emitted from outgoing particle moving at v/c|?0.3 were detected by the 
 34ALDc  Gamma-Ray detector Array with Position and Energy sensitivity (GRAPE)  
 34ALEc  consisting of segmented Ge detectors surrounding the liquid He target. 
